<title>SLOVENIA: ALPINE SKIING-MEN'S WORLD CUP GIANT SLALOM RESULTS.</title>
<headline>ALPINE SKIING-MEN'S WORLD CUP GIANT SLALOM RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>KRANJSKA GORA, Slovenia 1997-01-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Unofficial results</p>
<p>of a men's alpine skiing World Cup giant slalom on Sunday:</p>
<p>1. Michael Von Gruenigen (Switzerland) 2:13.42</p>
<p>(1:07.21/1:06.21)</p>
<p>2. Siegfried Voglreiter (Austria) 2:15.06 (1:07.91/1:07.15)</p>
<p>3. Kjetil Andre Aamodt (Norway) 2:15.78 (1:07.99/1:07.79)</p>
<p>4. Gerhard Koenigsrainer (Italy) 2:15.93 (1:08.38/1:07.55)</p>
<p>5. Ian Piccard (France) 2:15.96 (1:08.08/1:07.88)</p>
<p>6. Hans Knauss (Austria) 2:15.97 (1:08.01/1:07.96)</p>
<p>7. Heinz Schilchegger (Austria) 2:16.00 (1:08.61/1:07.39)</p>
<p>8. Thomas Grandi (Canada) 2:16.26 (1:08.24/1:08.02)</p>
<p>9. Jure Kosir (Slovenia) 2:16.27 (1:08.49/1:07.78)</p>
<p>10. Matteo Nana (Italy) 2:16.29 (1:08.21/1:08.08)</p>
<p>11. Harald Strand Nilsen (Norway) 2:16.30 (1:08.77/1:07.53)</p>
<p>12. Rainer Salzgeber (Austria) 2:16.34 (1:09.36/1:06.98)</p>
<p>13. Andreas Schifferer (Austria) 2:16.38 (1:08.98/1:07.40)</p>
<p>14. Hermann Maier (Austria) 2:16.43 (1:08.87/1:07.56)</p>
<p>15. Tom Stiansen (Norway) 2:16.72 (1:08.80/1:07.92)</p>
<p>16. Fredrik Nyberg (Sweden) 2:16.89 (1:08.70/1:08.19)</p>
<p>17. Paul Accola (Switzerland) 2:17.04 (1:09.14/1:07.90)</p>
<p>18. Christian Mayer (Austria) 2:17.05 (1:08.63/1:08.42)</p>
<p>19. Steve Locher (Switzerland) 2:17.15 (1:09.16/1:07.99)</p>
<p>20. Massimo Zucchelli (Italy) 2:17.23 (1:08.86/1:08.37)</p>
<p>21. Hans-Petter Buraas (Norway) 2:17.49 (1:08.95/1:08.54)</p>
<p>22. Mitja Kunc (Slovenia) 2:17.56 (1:09.04/1:08.52)</p>
<p>23. Tobias Barnersoi (Germany) 2:17.66 (1:08.91/1:08.75)</p>
<p>24. Joel Chenal (France) 2:17.69 (1:08.89/1:08.80)</p>
<p>25. Rene Mlekuz (Slovenia) 2:17.74 (1:09.11/1:08.63)</p>
<p>26. Achim Vogt (Liechtenstein) 2:17.87 (1:08.77/1:09.10)</p>
<p>27. Guenther Mader (Austria) 2:18.47 (1:09.09/1:09.38)</p>
<p>Results were later declared official.</p>
</text>
